course: dictionary
lesson: 15950
title: Unspoilt
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Unspoilt is made of un- and spoilt. The un- at the start means not, so unspoilt means not damaged or spoiled. «The beach was unspoilt, with clean sand and no buildings.» The beach has not been harmed by houses, litter or crowds.
explain: Unspoilt can also describe a person. «Even after she won the prize, Maya stayed unspoilt and kind to her friends.» Here it means Maya is still natural and nice, and money or fame has not made her selfish.
explain: Use the context to check. Ask: is this place still natural and beautiful, or is this person still natural and kind? If yes, unspoilt fits. Then try a simple word like natural in its place and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: «Unspoilt» means still natural and beautiful, not damaged by building, pollution or crowds.
fact: «Unspoilt» can also describe a person who is still natural and kind, not made selfish by money or fame.
fact: Unspoilt can also be spelled unspoiled, and both spellings are correct.
fact: In The Wind in the Willows, the River Bank is unspoilt countryside, while the Wild Wood is wild.
fact: Geography lessons often discuss how people can keep special places unspoilt for the future.
exercise: «The valley was unspoilt, with no roads or factories anywhere.» What does unspoilt mean here? | Full of cars and busy shops | Very old and falling down | *Still natural and beautiful, not damaged | Covered in snow
exercise: «Even after she became famous, Amy stayed unspoilt and kind.» What does unspoilt describe about Amy? | Her new clothes | Her famous name | *Her natural, kind nature, not made selfish by fame
exercise: Another correct spelling of unspoilt is which word? | unspilt | *unspoiled | unspoild
test: Which place is most likely to be unspoilt? | A busy shopping street full of traffic | A crowded beach covered in rubbish | A car park beside a motorway | *A quiet mountain lake with no litter or buildings around it
test: Why is the River Bank in The Wind in the Willows called unspoilt countryside? | It is full of crowds | *It is still natural and beautiful, not built over | It has heavy traffic | It is covered in snow
exam: The class wants to keep the local woods unspoilt. Which action helps most? | Cut down trees to make room for a playground | *Keep to the paths and take all litter home | Drop litter so the bins fill up | Build a new car park among the trees
